 "drivingQuestion": "Should the animal tithe, which sanctifies animals before and after it, precede the firstborn?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "The mishna's ordering stands",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "zevachim.89b.23",
   "daf": "89b",
   "sentenceId": 22,
   "he": "הַבְּכוֹר קוֹדֵם כּוּ׳. אַדְּרַבָּה – מַעֲשֵׂר קוֹדֵם, שֶׁכֵּן מְקַדֵּשׁ לְפָנָיו וּלְאַחֲרָיו! אֲפִילּוּ הָכִי, קְדוּשָּׁה מֵרֶחֶם עֲדִיפָא.",
   "en": "The mishna further teaches: «The firstborn» offering «precedes» the animal tithe offering because it is sanctified from the womb and is eaten only by the priests. The Gemara challenges: «On the contrary,» the animal «tithe» offering should «precede» the firstborn offering, «as» if one mistakenly called the ninth or eleventh animal that emerged from the pen the tenth, those animals that came out «before or after» the tenth are also «sanctified.» The Gemara explains: «Even so,» the fact that the firstborn is «sanctified from» the «womb» is of «greater» importance."
  }
 ],
